  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-25 (dev 2399d5ad7c; owner-requested re-check of the 17 actionable open P2 violated INV/META items; fixtures archived under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_10252026/). VERDICT: STALE-TEXT; still violated. Live repro with a stub sentence_transformers (logs each construction, then raises OSError, so nothing can download), empty HF_HOME, HF_HUB_OFFLINE unset, proxy at 127.0.0.1:9: `hypergumbo sketch` on a 2-file fixture exits 0 and logs 10 constructions -- unixcoder-base x2 and modernbert-embed-base x3 as {local_files_only: true, HF_HUB_OFFLINE: 1}, EACH followed by {local_files_only: false, HF_HUB_OFFLINE: null}, the download-allowed retry (sketch_embeddings.py:238-303, `return st_cls(model_name, **kwargs)` :293). Drift: cli.py ~4850 -> cmd_install_embeddings cli.py:5002-5062 (pip only); pin ~=5.2.2 -> EMBEDDINGS_REQUIREMENT sentence-transformers~=5.7 (cli.py:4963, e67891020a); load sites sketch.py:1524/1857, sketch_embeddings.py:1037/1821/1868/1928. UNDER-SCOPED: three install paths, not one -- install-embeddings, add-extras (_install_embeddings_impl cli.py:4064-4100) and pip install hypergumbo[embeddings] (README.md:124); none fetches weights and a pip extra cannot, so 'install-embeddings pre-fetches' alone cannot make the claim true -- only a refusing runtime fallback or a restated claim can. SECOND FALSE STATEMENT: the degradation warning (sketch_embeddings.py:176-183) says the weights 'are then cached under $HF_HOME' after install-embeddings, which caches no weights and exits early once ST>=5.7 is present. Side note: no negative caching, so an offline sketch tries 5 load pairs per process. Relation to WI-nuful (add-extras installs unpinned): different mechanism, same function _install_embeddings_impl -- a fix to either should touch both. README.md:124/155, SECURITY.md:38 and io-allowlist.yaml:596-613 already disclose this item. NOT checked: a real download (forbidden)."  # 02b3
